Tesla's 124-stall San Francisco Supercharger site will test whether open access sites can maintain uptime while serving mixed fleets. This is Tesla Shorts Time, Episode 574. Here's what you may have missed over the past week. Tesla's stock has stayed in the spotlight with steady volatility that keeps both long and short positions active. The company's push into AI and autonomy continues to draw the most attention from investors and observers.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:40.580
Google-related infrastructure questions around power and compute have surfaced in conversations about scaling. Those threads still feel like the ones shaping the near-term narrative.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:55.660
Owners in San Francisco report that full self-driving now handles roughly 95% of daily mileage on local roads. One Uber driver saw a remote safety score rise from 70 to 98% after switching to the software.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:08.460
Camera-based cabin monitoring allows drivers to look away from the road more naturally during routine trips. Community members note that the system stops for pedestrians the driver had missed on several occasions.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:24.100
San Francisco-based Uber driver, Rahula Hashimi, estimates the software controls about 95% of daily mileage. Local Club President Joe Jefferson pointed out that this update finally gives drivers the freedom to look at their passengers.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:32.240
The software offers highly customizable AI ranging from the laid-back chill mode to the assertive Mad Max setting.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:39.080
That performance on existing roads raises questions about the infrastructure needed to support growing fleets of those vehicles.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:52.640
Tesla filed plans for a 124-stall site in the city. The scale would rank among the largest urban supercharger locations. Open access for non-Tesla vehicles is expected at the new station.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:02:01.840
Site permitting and construction timelines remain the next visible steps. The planned open access site would rank among the largest urban locations.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:07.820
Next steps are permitting and construction and the question is whether mixed fleets can maintain uptime.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:20.300
That effort ties into a broader European open access rollout already underway. While the US site is still on the drawing board, a newly opened open access station in Ireland is already live.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:26.720
Tesla's Model 3 and Model Y took the top two spots on the Wall Street Journal's annual ranking.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:32.100
The result continues a pattern of Tesla vehicles leading the list in prior years.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.200
Manufacturing location data and parts sourcing percentages determine the ranking.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:43.480
The outcome highlights Tesla's domestic content levels relative to traditional Detroit automakers.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:51.000
Elon commented on the Wall Street Journal article that claims GM and Ford are fighting for the most American-made car.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.220
Tesla has won this award countless times, including this year.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:01.380
Domestic content strength stands in contrast with a real-world durability questions owners are tracking.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:11.280
After 25,000 miles, the battery health sits at an estimated 91%. The vehicle still delivers about 300 miles of range on a charge.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.620
The owner views the degradation rate as acceptable for daily use.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.360
Real-world capacity retention remains the key metric for long-term owners.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:26.220
The owner still sees roughly 300 miles of usable range and views the loss as acceptable.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:32.380
A first principles look notes that thermal management and driving patterns matter more than calendar aging.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.920
The data gives a clearer picture for used buyers and fleet operators than lab projections.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:45.780
Real-world battery performance feeds into larger questions about how Tesla communicates safety and reliability after incidents.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:50.380
Tesla posted that its vehicles are engineered to be the safest on the road.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:54.120
The statement followed a Model 3 incident reported in China.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.580
The company has emphasized structural design and sensor placement in prior safety discussions.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.900
No additional details on the specific crash were included in the post.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:08.420
The company restated vehicles are engineered to be the safest on the road.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.040
Emphasis falls on structural design and sensor placement.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:16.280
Labor issues in Sweden show another side of operational challenges.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:21.760
Tesla has offered buyouts to the remaining workers involved in the extended labor action.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.900
The strike has lasted longer than previous disputes at the company.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.840
The move aims to resolve the outstanding employment issues.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.620
No timeline for full resolution was provided in the report.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:37.880
Remaining workers on the extended labor action receive offers.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:41.820
The move aims to close out the dispute without a stated timeline.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:46.560
Market skepticism persists even as operational stories unfold.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:55.100
Short sellers have collected roughly $9 billion in gains on Tesla positions this year despite earlier predictions of their elimination.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:05:01.220
The contrast shows the trade remains active even after multiple quarters of mixed results.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:06.280
Position sizing and timing have allowed the group to stay profitable on the short side.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:11.160
Tesla's volatility continues to support both long and short strategies.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:18.880
The outcome underscores how market swings can sustain opposing bets even when public forecasts point in one direction.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:25.960
One account argues full self-driving progress will drive the next major shift in how investors value Tesla.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:31.360
Near-term software updates and regulatory feedback are cited as the key variables.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:37.540
The view positions autonomy milestones ahead of vehicle volume or energy growth in the short term.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:43.900
Errol Musk stated that optimist volume production could push Tesla's valuation near $8 trillion.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:49.440
The comment links humanoid robot output directly to long-term company size.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:54.240
No production volume or timeline details were provided alongside the projection.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:00.200
Tesla Roddy highlighted what it sees as the leading public worry when people are asked about AI.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:05.160
The post frames the concern as the dominant sentiment in casual conversations.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:09.940
The angle points to perception gaps between developers and everyday users.

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:21.680
Battery degradation data from daily driven model-wide vehicles shows that a 9% capacity loss after 25,000 miles still leaves usable range near 300 miles.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:31.880
This outcome sits between marketing claims of minimal fade and older concerns that lithium-ion packs would drop below 80% within the first two years.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:38.600
The measured result suggests owners can plan around gradual, predictable loss rather than sudden failure.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:45.420
Real-world testing under mixed driving conditions provides a clearer picture than accelerated lab cycles alone.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:53.320
The same data set also reveals that real-world discharge patterns and thermal management matter more than calendar aging alone.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:07:03.280
Vehicles that spend most miles on highway routes with steady state of charge windows retain more capacity than those subjected to frequent short trips and rapid charging.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:10.040
Tesla's thermal architecture appears to limit the worst-case scenarios that appeared in earlier pack generations.

